<title>INDIA: India 96/97 cotton output seen at 18 mln bales.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 cotton output seen at 18 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's cotton output in 1996/97 (September-August) is expected to be 18 million bales against 15.6 million in the previous year, Textiles Minister R. L. Jalappa said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The 96/97 (cotton) output is expected at a record 18 million bales,&quot; Jalappa told reporters.</p>
<p>One bale of cotton equals 170 kgs.</p>
<p>Traders had earlier estimated India's 1996/97 cotton crop at 16 million bales.</p>
</text>
